"**Short Text (Card Center)**: a short text printed in the middle of the "
"card, 10 characters at most; the acronym of your association for example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:275
msgid ""
"**Long Text (Bottom Line)**: a text printed at the bottom of the card, 65 "
"characters at most,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:276
msgid ""
"**Strip Text Color**: the color of the text written on the bottom strip,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:277
msgid ""
"**Active Member Color**, **Board Members Color** and **Honor Members "
"Color**: the color of the main texts and of the bottom strip, depending on "
"the status of the member; the honor color is used for benefactor and founder "
"members,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:278
msgid ""
"**Logo**: a logo for printing, if the one of the association does not suit,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:279
msgid ""
"**Allow members to print card ?**: members can download their own card, as "
"long as their membership is up to date,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:280
msgid "**Show title ?**: print the title (Mr., Mrs....) in front of the name,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:281
msgid ""
"**Address type**: what is printed under the name: email, zip code and town, "
"nickname, profession or member number,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:282
msgid ""
"**Year**: the year printed on the card. It can be a year, two years "
"separated with a slash (*2026/2027*), or ``DEADLINE`` to print the end of "
"membership of each member,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:283
msgid ""
"margins, spacing, width and height of the cards on the page, in millimeters."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:285
msgid "Colors are written in hexadecimal notation, ``#RRGGBB``."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:290
msgid "Dynamic fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:294
msgid ""
"You can add your own fields to the preferences, for information about your "
"association that Galette does not know about: a registration number, a bank "
"account number, the name of the president..."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:296
msgid ""
"Create them from **Configuration**, then **Dynamic fields**, choosing the "
"**Settings** form; see :ref:`dynamic fields <dynamic_fields>`. They are then "
"displayed in this tab, and can be used as variables in :ref:`emails contents "
"<emails_contents>` and in :ref:`PDF models <pdf_models>`."
msgstr ""

# 59f3f24b2678418cbaf8264cb61c56f5
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:301
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

# e7bfe69983544648b9d5d714327b8776
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:307
msgid ""
"Complex password rules are not user friendly; but security is mainly never :)"
msgstr ""

# 570e17799c1d497eb9af2e95ad2780aa
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:309
msgid ""
"Of course, all passwords should be as secure as possible, but this is "
"especially true for all accounts that have privileges (staff, admin, super-"
"admin); you may explain your users why this is important."
msgstr ""

# fff95ddfffec46638e5339356186deef
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:311
msgid "You can enforce some rules for members (and super-admin) passwords:"
msgstr ""

# ee8bcb4532c34c1ba889ddf0a74dd41c
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:313
msgid "minimum length (6 characters or more),"
msgstr ""

# 79fe63911b564890802adcf767131707
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:314
msgid "minimum \"strength\","
msgstr ""

# 2b3992cafb854047b5fdcbf88d40217e
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:315
msgid "blacklist,"
msgstr ""

# e85e35e110744770a03663beb062e501
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:316
msgid "no personal information."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:318
msgid "Galette settings, security tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:323
msgid ""
"The **Test a password:** field, at the bottom of the tab, checks any "
"password against the values currently selected; do not forget to save your "
"preferences once you are happy with the result."
msgstr ""

# 053343e209714fffabbdaecff65a81e5
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:325
msgid ""
"Length is still the only rule that is active per default, just configure the "
"number of characters required. On passwords fields, failures will be "
"displayed on the fly; as well as a \"strength meter\" displayed for "
"information."
msgstr ""

# 4209b4bc1cd448219d37156cda7e420a
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:329
msgid ""
"If you enable password checks, it is not possible to know if some of "
"existing ones does not respect them. Galette will display a warning at login "
"if checks are not respected, but login will still be possible!"
msgstr ""

# 78e1ec1f228146f2be3cf46d52ee679f
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:331
msgid ""
"But wait... Password security is important, but Galette does not enforce "
"nothing! Isn't that dumb? Well, not really. For tests or entirely private "
"instances, security may be less important; and in some cases, being too "
"restrictive may be an issue for your users; that's why this is up to you to "
"secure as needed; just like using SSL or not :)"
msgstr ""

# c2ebfee2cf554c3db4d358329ac44fed
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:334
msgid "Password strength"
msgstr ""

# 98eae32c24b94720be85c712e0d0976c
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:336
msgid "Password strength calculation is quite simple. It is based on 4 rules:"
msgstr ""

# e604d81f64d148bdaac9e4e2dba4edbf
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:338
msgid "contains lower case characters,"
msgstr ""

# f2745eaadb224df2bdc88c3657d87438
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:339
msgid "contains upper case characters,"
msgstr ""

# dcca5661bd7845e8b4cc6576ca0ab932
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:340
msgid "contains number,"
msgstr ""

# 6134e0ab5cca42a58cf6d1c753008529
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:341
msgid "contains special characters."
msgstr ""

# 5ed15ee7aa7e4b24a0b20b61e2c3e0a6
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:343
msgid "You can choose between 5 values for strength configuration:"
msgstr ""

# 5280643fa53246d6bfa3264c699adc4d
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:345
msgid ""
"**none**: (default): disables strength checks and check for personal "
"information,"
msgstr ""

# 394c5519cf9b464bba1968b6d28fcaa3
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:346
msgid ""
"**weaker**: enables check for personal information, only one of the rule is "
"mandatory,"
msgstr ""

# 11f3d1b16316428cbb6849ea5a1391c7
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:347
msgid "**medium**: two rules are mandatory,"
msgstr ""

# 0b54fe121ee34df78ed9a1e055c3e0fe
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:348
msgid "**strong**: three rules are mandatory,"
msgstr ""

# 519a18052f774c3ebf7f29e782153010
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:349
msgid "**very strong**: the four rules are mandatory."
msgstr ""

# 7165d4847cfc48a9b5763006e04d8f26
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:352
msgid "Blacklisted passwords"
msgstr ""

# c932b59f38f740b4a9df457047124454
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:354
msgid ""
"A default list of 500 common passwords is provided as a blacklist you can "
"enable, \"galette\" is also blacklisted."
msgstr ""

# ac46d13e12dc477586e4bfa8e5bf1970
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:358
msgid ""
"The ``galette/data/blacklist.txt`` file is used to list blacklisted terms "
"(one per line). You can provide your own file, we advice you to complete the "
"existing one."
msgstr ""

# 881799d56851496c80b3607662af7717
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:361
msgid "Personal information as password"
msgstr ""

# 5c44c938be1c41829b70b48cbd1c9274
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:363
msgid ""
"This check rely on strength activation (all but **none** level). For the "
"super-admin account, this will just ensure you are not using login as "
"password. For standard accounts, there are several information involved:"
msgstr ""

# 41e3dc76750c4e95a7ec5c0982076aef
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:365
msgid "name,"
msgstr ""

# 892a5679ce1c42938e623447c0d9c57b
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:366
msgid "surname,"
msgstr ""

# 5b9ebd575687433bad8d1a1b105461e1
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:367
msgid "nickname,"
msgstr ""

# 723c1559216645e49936bc7f80fe1b1a
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:368
msgid "login,"
msgstr ""

# 85969edce28f44e09d60e30f62052d17
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:369
msgid "email,"
msgstr ""

# 0c720bac6f224edc9093e8fe62f94025
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:370
msgid "birthdate,"
msgstr ""

# 61da7c7894d942b682788f9adb077df1
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:371
msgid "town"
msgstr ""

# 810e9f55a31f48ea8ea2f1342c8331b1
#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:373
msgid ""
"Basically, user cannot use verbatim any of those information as password. "
"Some possible combinations are also checked, like surname and name couple "
"(or name and surname), first letter of surname with name, etc. Birthdate "
"will be checked in different formats as well (localized, international, and "
"some variants)."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:378
msgid "Two-factor authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:382
msgid ""
"Marked **experimental**: it is complete and tested, but it is new, and the "
"interface may still change. It is disabled by default; nothing happens until "
"you choose otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:384
msgid ""
"A password is a single factor: whoever knows it is in. Two-factor "
"authentication asks, right after the password, for a six digits code that "
"changes every thirty seconds and comes from an application on the user own "
"phone or computer. A stolen password is then not enough anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:386
msgid ""
"Galette implements the TOTP standard (:rfc:`6238`), the one every "
"authenticator application speaks; no third party service is involved, and "
"nothing leaves your server."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:388
msgid "Two policies are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:390
msgid "**disabled** (default): nothing changes, nobody is asked for a code,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:391
msgid ""
"**optional**: everybody may enable it from their own account, nobody has to."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:393
msgid ""
"Making the second factor **compulsory** — for administrators and staff "
"members, or for everyone — is written and tested, but it is not offered yet: "
"under a compulsory policy, a server clock that drifts or an enrolment that "
"goes wrong puts a whole association outside its own instance, and the only "
"way back is a command in the database. It is planned for a later version, "
"once the optional policy has been used in the field."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:395
msgid ""
"Since nobody is forced to enrol, administrators and staff members — the "
"accounts that can read the civil status, the addresses and the financial "
"data of every member — are invited to set a second factor up when they log "
"in, with a **Later** and a **Do not ask again** button. Declining is "
"remembered in a cookie of the browser, so the invitation comes back on a new "
"browser, or after a year."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:399
msgid ""
"Switching the policy back to **disabled** does not delete anything. Codes "
"are no longer asked for, and the second factors already enabled start being "
"asked for again as soon as you enable a policy back. While the policy is "
"disabled, the pages to enable a second factor answer nothing: a factor "
"enrolled then would never be asked for."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:401
msgid ""
"The super administrator is covered as well, as any other account. As it is "
"not a member, it has no recovery codes; see :ref:`what to do should you lose "
"it <faq_2fa>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:403
msgid ""
"Members enable and manage their own second factor from their account; this "
"is described in :ref:`the members part of this manual <man_2fa>`. "
"Administrators and staff members can :ref:`reset the second factor of a "
"member <member_2fa_reset>` who lost it."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:408
msgid "Authentication attempts"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:412
msgid ""
"To protect accounts against people trying passwords one after the other, "
"Galette counts the failed logins. After too many failures, further attempts "
"are refused for a while, even with the right password. The same applies to "
"password recovery requests and to self registrations."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:414
msgid "By default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:416
msgid "5 failed logins on one account, from one address, within 15 minutes,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:417
msgid "30 failed logins from one address, on any account, within 15 minutes,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:418
msgid "100 failed logins on one account, from anywhere, within a day,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:419
msgid "3 password recovery requests within an hour,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:421
msgid ""
"get further attempts refused for 15 minutes. Those thresholds and durations "
"can be changed from the :ref:`advanced configuration <advanced_config>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:423
msgid ""
"**Configuration**, then **Authentication attempts** lists what is refused "
"right now: what is counted, the account, the address, the number of failures "
"and until when attempts are refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:425
msgid "Authentication attempts currently refused"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:430
msgid ""
"When a member tells you they cannot log in anymore, look here: **Lift** lets "
"them try again at once, and **Lift them all** clears the whole list."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:433
msgid "Super administrator credentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:437
msgid ""
"The super administrator login and password are no longer in the preferences. "
"Once logged in as super administrator, go to **My account**, then **My "
"information**. Galette asks for the current password before saving a new one."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/preferences.rst:439
msgid ""
"Should that password be lost, it can be changed :ref:`from the command line "
"<cli_superadmin_password>`."
msgstr ""
